# Production variables.
#
# Every variable below is OPTIONAL for local development. With none of them set,
# `npm run dev` uses an embedded Postgres under ./.crucible and the Hugging Face
# and arXiv public APIs. You need no API key to run the core product.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in only what you need. Never commit it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Persistence (required in production)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# A hosted Postgres connection string. Neon, Supabase, Vercel Postgres or any
# other Postgres 14+ works over the wire protocol.
#
# Crucible refuses to start a production-mode process without this. It will not
# silently fall back to the embedded adapter, because a serverless filesystem is
# not a durable store and every visitor's rows would vanish on redeploy.
#
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/db?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=

# Optional: namespace every table, so one database can host several instances
# without their rows colliding.
# DATABASE_SCHEMA=crucible

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment identity
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public origin, used for canonical URLs, OpenGraph tags, the sitemap, the
# exported dossier links and the agent manifest. Set this to the real alias
# after the first deploy so nothing points at a guessed hostname.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-alias.vercel.app

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development escape hatch — never set this on a deployment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Allows the embedded adapter to run inside a production-mode process. It exists
# solely so `next build && next start` can be verified locally against the real
# production artifact. Setting it on a deployment would make your data
# ephemeral, which is the exact failure the guard above exists to prevent.
# CRUCIBLE_ALLOW_EMBEDDED_STORE=1

# Where the embedded database keeps its files when running locally.
# CRUCIBLE_PGLITE_DIR=.crucible/pgdata